X128 — ΣΤΟΙΧΟΘΈΤΗΣ: alignment-aware fixed-width columnar blocks. NEW CODEC, SHIPPED OFF.
Branch arena/6adc24e4-kompkernel from 77e5e02. Node 22.22.3, o200k_base, OMEGA_DET=1.

WHY IT IS NEW. ΣΤΉΛΗ (steli.ts) cannot express a RIGHT-ALIGNED cell: `sliceRow`
does `const f = seg.trim()` and `steliRebuildRow` writes the field back at an
absolute offset, so every cell comes out left-aligned; its offset candidates also
come from `startsOf`, which only fires after TWO OR MORE spaces. Every numeric
column in `ps aux` / `ls -l` / `free -m` / `kubectl get` is right-aligned, so
ΣΤΉΛΗ returns null on all of them. ΚΑΝΏΝ (kanon.ts) is a different thing — a gate
over HYLE's fold lattice with a fixed DAEDALUS arm, and a frontier PARENT.
ΣΤΟΙΧΟΘΈΤΗΣ adds one symbol per column (alignment) and is a pure pre-transform.

CORRECTNESS CONTRACT. Alignment is not guessed: column j is 'L' only if every row
starts that field at the same offset, 'R' only if every row ends it there, else the
block is rejected. Widths come from the gap equations
    gap_ij = [a_j=='L' ? w_j-|f_ij| : 0] + [a_j+1=='R' ? w_j+1-|f_i,j+1| : 0]
and EVERY candidate block is rebuilt and compared byte-for-byte to the source
before acceptance; `stoichothetesTransform` then re-checks the whole text with its
own inverse and returns null if it does not round-trip. A bad width can therefore
only lose compression, never fidelity.

