2. END-TO-END THROUGH THE REAL FRONTIER (bench/x126/x128-stoichothetes-e2e.ts)
   lane                     M(baseline)  M(with ΣΤΟΙΧΟΘΈΤΗΣ)   Δ     round-trip
   kubectl-get-pods.txt          303            327           +24      EXACT
   psql-output.txt               230            268           +38      EXACT
   df-h.txt                      160            243           +83      EXACT

   VERDICT: NOT PARETO. It reclaims real whitespace (pad-mass 733 on kubectl) and
   still loses end-to-end, and the reason is the finding: the frontier's dictionary
   ALREADY recovers aligned space runs as shared rules, so the padding was never
   costing what it appears to cost, and the ~40-token geometry marker is paid on
   top. Explicit padding removal is redundant with the existing stack.

3. DISCLOSURE — a tracked file was clobbered and restored during this work.
   `src/lib/omega/kanon.ts` already existed (it is a frontier parent, imported at
   tagstack.ts:33) and was overwritten by a first draft of this mechanism that
   reused the name. It was restored with `git checkout -- src/lib/omega/kanon.ts`
   before any build that referenced it ran; the frontier re-verification of §5 ran
   BEFORE the overwrite and is unaffected. The rewrite is named ΣΤΟΙΧΟΘΈΤΗΣ.

4. WHERE THE REMAINING HEADROOM ACTUALLY IS (measured, not argued)
   Lanes that reach the numeric/columnar ops compress 75-80 %:
       prices.csv 582 -> 119 (79.6 %), metrics.tsv 811 -> 198 (75.6 %),
       kubectl 1006 -> 303, vix/aapl/dump/psql/df via ΚΑΝΏΝ.
   Lanes that only reach the dictionary compress 67-70 %:
       ps-aux-real 3054 -> 988 (67.6 %), apt-real 2739 -> 816 (70.2 %).
   The 8-10 point gap is the headroom, and it sits in VARIABLE-WIDTH ops listings.
   ΣΤΟΙΧΟΘΈΤΗΣ was the attempt to close it by attacking alignment; it failed.
   What that leaves: the variable-width lanes may simply be at their dictionary
   limit, because their residual is free text (the COMMAND column of ps aux, the
   package names and versions of apt list) which no dictionary can touch.
